# Trivy CVE ignore list
# Only suppress CVEs that cannot be fixed from our side
# (OS packages without Debian backports, disputed advisories, or platform-specific issues)

# ── zlib / MiniZip ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CVE-2023-45853: MiniZip integer overflow — explicitly noted by NVD as not a supported
# part of the zlib library; Debian has not backported a fix for this disputed advisory.
CVE-2023-45853

# ── GNU tar (Debian OS package) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# CVE-2005-2541: tar extraction side-effects — 20-year-old informational advisory,
# no patch exists; only affects manual user behaviour, not automated pipelines.
CVE-2005-2541

# TEMP-0290435-0B57B5: rmt command side-effects — Debian tracking entry, no CVE fix.
TEMP-0290435-0B57B5

# ── esbuild (development build tool, not runtime) ───────────────────────────
# GHSA-g7r4-m6w7-qqqr: dev-server path traversal on Windows only.
# esbuild is a build-time dev tool; the production Docker image does not run
# esbuild's development server, and our CI runners are Linux-only.
GHSA-g7r4-m6w7-qqqr
